<article class="env-lemma" id="09T5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09T5">Lemma <span data-tag="09T5">13.30.3</span>.</a> Let $F : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ and $G : \mathcal{B} \to \mathcal{A}$ be functors of abelian categories such that $F$ is a right adjoint to $G$. If the derived functors $RF : D(\mathcal{A}) \to D(\mathcal{B})$ and $LG : D(\mathcal{B}) \to D(\mathcal{A})$ exist, then $RF$ is a right adjoint to $LG$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
